1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,833
Agentic coding made us faster.

2
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:10,867
A whole week's code before
breakfast.

3
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:15,900
Forty pull requests. I tagged the
team.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:21,433
The lead said: We need time to
review them properly.

5
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:26,466
Of course! Quality comes first.

6
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:31,500
So while they reviewed them...

7
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:36,533
I made ten more.

8
00:00:36,733 --> 00:00:41,566
Ten more!

9
00:00:41,766 --> 00:00:46,600
And they were doing good reviews!

10
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:51,633
Checking edge cases. Finding real
bugs.

11
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:57,343
One guy spent two hours
understanding a race condition.

12
00:00:57,543 --> 00:01:02,935
During those two hours, I created
three new services.

13
00:01:03,135 --> 00:01:07,968
He was still on the first service!

14
00:01:08,168 --> 00:01:13,001
Then they organized a review day.

15
00:01:13,201 --> 00:01:18,035
No coding. Everyone clears the
backlog.

16
00:01:18,235 --> 00:01:23,068
Everyone except my agents.

17
00:01:23,268 --> 00:01:28,101
By lunch they'd reviewed fifty.

18
00:01:28,301 --> 00:01:33,134
The queue had grown by ninety.

19
00:01:33,334 --> 00:01:38,168
And they said: We're making good
progress.

20
00:01:38,368 --> 00:01:43,201
Good progress!

21
00:01:43,401 --> 00:01:48,234
They asked me to help.

22
00:01:48,434 --> 00:01:53,267
I built a dashboard to track the
backlog.

23
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:58,301
Then I tagged them to review it.

24
00:01:58,501 --> 00:02:03,334
They asked for smaller pull
requests.

25
00:02:03,534 --> 00:02:08,367
Very reasonable. Easier to
understand.

26
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:13,401
So I split the next one into three.

27
00:02:13,601 --> 00:02:18,434
Three pull requests! Three reviews!

28
00:02:18,634 --> 00:02:23,467
Three pipelines!

29
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:28,500
The lead said: This is like
Sisyphus.

30
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:33,534
I said: No, he had one rock.

31
00:02:33,734 --> 00:02:38,567
Our rocks create more rocks.

32
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:43,600
At five they said: We'll finish
tomorrow.

33
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:48,634
Tomorrow!

34
00:02:48,834 --> 00:02:53,667
I left the agents running overnight.

35
00:02:53,867 --> 00:02:58,700
They'll be reviewing until
Tomorrowland.

36
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:03,733
Management asked if we'd saved time.

37
00:03:03,933 --> 00:03:08,767
I said: I've saved loads.

38
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:13,800
Their time? I've booked the next six
years.
